=== EXPLICIT B(k): far-limit gap vs bounded global max ===

--- k=8 ---
  M_8   (bounded global max)   = 0.32721  at [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
  M_7 (max over (k-1)-sets)  = 0.14762  at [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
  far-limit upper bound = M_7+1/7 = 0.29048
  cap_8 = 0.38153
  GAP  M_8 - (M_7+1/7) = +0.03673  (far limit BELOW global max -- contraction in limit)

--- k=9 ---
  M_9   (bounded global max)   = 0.41616  at [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]
  M_8 (max over (k-1)-sets)  = 0.32721  at [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
  far-limit upper bound = M_8+1/7 = 0.47007
  cap_9 = 0.49426
  GAP  M_9 - (M_8+1/7) = -0.05391  (NO gap -- limit could match max!)

INTERPRETATION:
  If GAP>0, every far element contracts strictly below the bounded global
  max in the w->inf limit. An Erdos-Turan rate |meas - LIM| <= D/w then
  gives explicit B(k) = ceil(D / GAP): for w>B(k), meas(S7) < M_k <= cap_k.
